From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <contact@volta.audio>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 16:23:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: route through headless wsi + iOS-path Present + portable
 test fixes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Headless wsi on our aarch64-windows target
   src/util/meson.build: select wsi_{window,monitor}_headless.cpp for the
   aarch64-windows cross-build (same files dxmt_native already uses on
   macOS). Keeps wsi_platform_win32.cpp for Windows-ABI aligned_malloc.
   Without this, every wsi::* call lands in user32 and returns garbage on
   our Wine (no real window manager) — getClientRect gives uninitialized
   stack data, isMinimized says yes, etc.

2. iOS Present path
   src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp Present1: under DXMT_IOS, treat the
   single iOS Metal surface as always visible + foregrounded. Without
   this, wsi::isMinimized(hWnd) returned true for our fake HWND, Present
   short-circuited with DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED (0x087A0001), and no frames
   ever reached the CAMetalLayer.

3. Test portability (applies everywhere, not just iOS)
   tests/dx11/*.cpp: LoadIconW/LoadCursorW took `0` for HINSTANCE and
   `IDI_APPLICATION`/`IDC_ARROW` for the name arg. MSVC accepts the
   implicit conversions; clang++ does not. Cast to `(HINSTANCE)nullptr`
   and `(LPCWSTR)IDI_APPLICATION` / `(LPCWSTR)IDC_ARROW`.

4. iOS-specific test scaffolding (dx11_cube.cpp only for now)
   - Skip the PeekMessageW loop — no real message queue on iOS, our
     Wine's user32 has no backing driver.
   - Hardcode 1024x768 swapchain + viewport — GetClientRect on our
     fake HWND returns uninitialized stack data; at Width/Height=0
     DXGI uses GetClientRect which made the backbuffer invalid.
   - Replace OutputDebugStringA/W with fprintf — OutputDebugString
     blocked on our Wine without the DBG_PRINTEXCEPTION_C path wired.

Validated on iPhone: dx11_cube renders the RGB-gradient spinning cube
at 60fps with depth testing, constant-buffer transform, index buffer,
interpolated vertex colors. Full D3D11 feature coverage well beyond
the earlier triangle.

Real games will still need a proper winios.drv to replace Wine's
missing display driver — these per-test patches are test-scaffold
fixes only.

